{"body":"## Accepted result and scope\n\nThe original finitely presented counterexample questions for conjugation-invariant norms remain **unsolved, 5/5**. The five partial results establish bounded derived subgroups and both norm dichotomies for finitely generated virtually metabelian groups; inheritance through split abelian extensions; an exact rational stable-norm algorithm under a supplied bounded-derived promise; and a selected braid word detected in every finite truncation but bounded in the infinite-distance shift group. The infinite presentation does not establish abstract non-finite-presentability. The split and promise hypotheses, ordinary versus partial quasimorphisms, ambient metrics and finite-size dependencies are retained.\n\n## Adversarial verification\n\nRoot reconstructed all five proofs, read all executable sources and primary theorem hypotheses, and reproduced345888 author and47964 historical assertions. Distinct algebra, integral-LP and braid families and a source-first baseline were checked. A new candidate-free source-first whole-package reviewer found no mandatory repair at corrected head420ffdfbb021c5a9378ccbbac198a13a4508dfad. Root reproduced all ten complete candidate/control streams byte exactly, including251278 new post-candidate controls, and verified44 Git objects,66 nested bindings,64 historical Git bindings, four links and23 bounded final review outputs. Numerical controls support the written arguments; they do not replace universal proofs or credited signature/displacement theorems.\n\nSix fresh original primary PDFs match historical bindings. Two legacy PNG byte bindings remain unavailable; public replay checks0/8 optional raw-source bindings. Three supplementary fresh primary sources are separately credited. The Muranov non-finite-presentability attribution is supported by BGKM manuscript page5; literal OWR page199 gives two-generation. BK/GG signature conventions differ in sign and agree in absolute value2. No current worldwide open-status or novelty certification is claimed.\n\n[Acceptance decision](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/main/draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr380_30002762/ACCEPTANCE_DECISION.md); [fresh whole-package adversary](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/main/draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr380_30002762/clean_final_adversary/REPORT.md). Original head9946a67cf8a1f7e3130d2a12de902db05875283a; reviewed head420ffdfbb021c5a9378ccbbac198a13a4508dfad. The queue repair preserves every other accepted outcome, with actual integration checked again immediately before and after merge.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in research, drafting, verification and adversarial review. This is unrefereed work, not external human peer review. Accept as scoped partial progress; no paper, Zenodo deposit, DOI, tracker row or release.\n","headRefOid":"420ffdfbb021c5a9378ccbbac198a13a4508dfad","isDraft":false,"mergeCommit":{"oid":"9139294727b826926797b26efdd6edc2ca0d1f21"},"mergeStateStatus":"UNKNOWN","mergeable":"UNKNOWN","mergedAt":"2026-10-03T05:44:27Z","state":"MERGED","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/380"}
